---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/astro/Prose.astro";
import { SITE, DISCLAIMER } from "@/lib/site";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<PageLayout
  title="About ChatWrapped"
  description="Who builds ChatWrapped, why it exists, how it stays free and private, and where it is going next. An independent open-source conversation analytics project."
  path="/about/"
>
  <Prose />
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-white">About ChatWrapped</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-zinc-300">
      ChatWrapped started with a simple observation: our most meaningful conversations happen in
      chat apps, and then they scroll away. “Wrapped”-style recaps proved that people love seeing
      their year in data — but your chats deserve the same treatment without handing a stranger’s
      server your most personal files.
    </p>

    <div class="prose-cw">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        A free, open-source, browser-based tool that turns WhatsApp and Telegram exports into
        accurate statistics, personalized story recaps and social-ready share cards. It runs
        entirely as a static site — there is no backend, no database and no account system, which is
        also why it can never lose your data: it never has it.
      </p>

      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Local by architecture, not by promise.</strong> Nothing to upload to, by design — verifiable
          in the network tab and by automated tests.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Honest numbers.</strong> Every metric is documented with definitions, exclusions and
          edge cases. Ties are labeled; missing data is admitted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fun without manipulation.</strong> Stories and awards are playful activity facts — never
          fake streak-pressure or psychological claims.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Free forever for the core.</strong> Static hosting on GitHub Pages costs nothing; there
          are no paid tiers to gate.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Technology</h2>
      <p>
        Astro + React with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, hand-rolled SVG charts, a Canvas card renderer,
        Web Workers for parsing and analytics, JSZip for recap exports, Vitest and Playwright for
        the test suite — deployed as static files. The full architecture is documented in the
        <a href={SITE.repo}>repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Telegram HTML exports and WhatsApp media ZIPs are not parsed yet (JSON and TXT are).
        </li>
        <li>
          Timezone information is absent from exports, so day/hour buckets reflect the exporter’s
          clock.
        </li>
        <li>Story slides adapt to your data — small chats simply produce fewer slides.</li>
        <li>Very large exports (hundreds of MB) are beyond the tested limits.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Roadmap ideas</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>More platforms (Instagram, Signal, iMessage via exports) as format testing allows.</li>
        <li>Telegram HTML export support.</li>
        <li>Additional card layouts and theme refinements.</li>
        <li>More languages for stopwords and UI.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contributing</h2>
      <p>
        Bug reports, parser fixtures and theme ideas are welcome at <a href={SITE.repo}
          >{SITE.repo}</a
        > — see CONTRIBUTING.md in the repository. Please never attach real chat exports to issues; fixtures
        are synthetic.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-6 text-center">
      <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white">Try it in 30 seconds</p>
      <p class="mt-1 mb-4 text-sm text-zinc-400">
        No export needed — the sample data is one click away.
      </p>
      <a
        href={`${base}/app/`}
        class="inline-block rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-600 px-6 py-3 font-bold text-white"
        >Open the analyzer →</a
      >
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">{DISCLAIMER}</p>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
